course: french
lesson: 7
title: Numbers 21 to 69
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Once you know the tens, French numbers up to 69 are like Lego: take a ten, click on a unit with a hyphen, and you have a number.
explain: The tens are vingt (20), trente (30), quarante (40), cinquante (50) and soixante (60); the last four all end in -ante or -ente.
explain: The ones are special: 21, 31, 41, 51 and 61 say "and one", so 21 is vingt et un, while 22 is just vingt-deux.
explain: Picture a bus in Dublin: Liam calls it "trente-un" and the French driver laughs, "Trente et un, mon grand!"
explain: For your age, French uses "have", not "be": j'ai neuf ans means "I am nine", but word for word "I have nine years".
fact: The tens: vingt ("van") 20, trente ("trahnt") 30, quarante ("ka-RAHNT") 40, cinquante ("sank-AHNT") 50, soixante ("swa-SAHNT") 60.
fact: In soixante the x sounds like s.
fact: 21, 31, 41, 51 and 61 use et un: vingt et un, trente et un, quarante et un, cinquante et un, soixante et un.
fact: The other numbers just join the ten and the unit with a hyphen: vingt-deux (22), trente-quatre (34), quarante-quatre (44), soixante-cinq (65).
fact: In quarante and quatre, qu says "k", with no w: quarante-quatre is "ka-rahnt-KATR".
fact: French phone numbers have ten digits and are read in pairs: 06 12 34 56 78 is zéro six, douze, trente-quatre, cinquante-six, soixante-dix-huit.
fact: Prices are said as euros then cents, often without the word cents: un euro vingt is €1.20; euro takes an s for more than one: deux euros.
fact: J'ai neuf ans means "I am nine"; je suis neuf would mean "I am new".
fact: Combien ? means "how many?" or "how much?"; Tu as combien de bonbons ? means "How many sweets have you got?" and wants a number for an answer.
fact: Un numéro is a number on a shirt, a bus, a house or a ticket: le numéro vingt-trois is number 23.
fact: seize is 16 but soixante is 60; the longer word is the bigger number.
fact: Slang here: "canny" (Newcastle) means very or nice; "no cap" means honestly; "our kid" (Manchester) means my brother or sister; "bare" (London) means lots of; "boss" (Liverpool) means great; "heaps" (Australia) means very; "y'all" (Texas) means you all.
exercise: Daniel writes "vingt-un" for 21. What is right? | vingt et un | vingt-un | vingt-et-une | un-vingt
exercise: Which is 22? | vingt-deux | vingt et deux | deux-vingt | vingt-deuze
exercise: Which list shows the tens from 30 to 60 in order? | trente, quarante, cinquante, soixante | trente, quarante, soixante, cinquante | treize, quatorze, quinze, seize | trois, quatre, cinq, six
exercise: How does the x in soixante sound? | like an s | like ks | like z | silent
exercise: Ruby's penpal reads her number in pairs. What does "trente-quatre" stand for? | 34 | 304 | 43 | 3 and 4 said one at a time
exercise: The lady says "Un euro vingt." What does Toby pay? | €1.20 | €21 | €20.01 | €120
exercise: Harry is asked "Tu as quel âge ?" How should he say he is nine? | J'ai neuf ans. | Je suis neuf. | J'ai neuf. | Je neuf ans.
exercise: What does je suis neuf really mean? | I am new | I am nine | I have nine | I am ninth
exercise: How do you say quarante-quatre (44)? | "ka-rahnt-KATR" | "kwah-rant-KWAH-truh" | "kwa-RAHNT-kwa-tray" | "ka-RAN-ka-TRAY"
exercise: What is 31 in French? | trente et un | trente-un | trois-un | treize-un
exercise: Which number also uses et? | 51 | 52 | 15 | 25
exercise: The kids ask Sophie "Tu as combien de bonbons ?" What do they want? | A number of sweets | The flavour of the sweets | A sweet for themselves | Where she bought them
exercise: What does le numéro vingt-trois mean? | number 23 | number 203 | the 23rd of the month | twenty-three numbers
exercise: Ella counts down: quarante-neuf, then? | quarante-huit | quarante | cinquante | trente-huit
exercise: How many rabbits are in "Les soixante-cinq lapins"? | 65 | 16 and 5 | 56 | 605
exercise: Which is bigger? | soixante | seize | quinze | quatorze
test: Daniel moans, "Why's 21 got 'and' in it? Man, that's canny daft." ("Canny" means very.) What's the rule? | 21, 31, 41, 51 and 61 use et un; others use a hyphen | Every number in the twenties uses et, like vingt et deux | Only 21 uses et, because it is the first of the twenties | It is a typo; French teachers argue about it a lot
test: Chloe says "soixante sounds like a sneeze, no cap." ("No cap" means honestly.) She says "swax-ant". What's the fix? | "swa-SAHNT", the x says s | "swa-KSANT", with a clear ks | "soy-XANT", with an English x | "swa-ZAHNT", the x says z
test: Ruby says, "Our kid, she's reading out a lottery." Her penpal said "zéro six, douze, trente-quatre". What did she mean? | 06 12 34 | 0 6 1 2 3 4 | 6 12 30 4 | 06 21 43
test: A cartoon English boy in Paris says "Je suis dix!" to show he is ten. What should he say? | J'ai dix ans. | Je suis dix ans. | J'ai dix. | Je dix ans.
test: Olivia in Chicago reads quarante-quatre with "kwah" sounds. Her teacher says, "Close, but drop the w's." Why? | French qu says just "k" | French q is always silent | French w is said like v | French quarante has no q
test: The French driver laughs, "Trente et un, mon grand !" when Liam says "trente-un". What would 41 be? | quarante et un | quarante-un | quatorze-un | quatre-un
test: Sophie says "Like, bare amount" when asked how many sweets. ("Bare" means lots of.) What would a French kid say for 25? | J'en ai vingt-cinq. | J'ai beaucoup combien. | Vingt et cinq, merci. | Cinq-vingt bonbons.
test: Oliver goes, "Proper boss, I know them now." ("Boss" means great.) He hears "le numéro dix-sept" at the match. Which shirt is it? | 17 | 7 | 70 | 10
test: Ella says counting backwards is "heaps hard". What number comes right before quarante-sept? | quarante-six | quarante-huit | quatorze-six | trente-six
test: Ollie's family in Texas reads "soixante" as "sixteen". Why is that wrong? | Sixteen is seize; soixante is sixty | Soixante is sixty-six, not sixteen | Soixante is six hundred in French | They are right; both start with s
test: ★★★ Mum pays "deux euros cinquante" for bread and "un euro vingt" for a croissant. How much in all? | €3.70 | €3.25 | €3.50 | €4.70
test: ★★★ Which number word is spelled right? | soixante et un | vingt et deux | vingt et six | trente-un
exam: Which of the following statements most accurately characterises the formation of the numbers twenty-one, thirty-one and forty-one? | Each is formed by the conjunction et preceding un | Each is formed by a hyphen alone, without any conjunction | Each is formed by placing the unit before the ten | Each possesses a distinct single word
exam: Identify the correct French expression of the statement "I am nine years of age". | J'ai neuf ans | Je suis neuf | Je suis neuf ans | J'ai neuf
exam: Select the response consistent with the established facts concerning French telephone numbers. | They comprise ten digits, customarily pronounced in pairs | They comprise six digits, pronounced singly | They comprise ten digits, pronounced in groups of three | They are pronounced in English by statute
exam: It is given that a price is announced as "un euro vingt". Ascertain the sum payable. | One euro and twenty cents | Twenty-one euros | One hundred and twenty euros | Twenty euros and one cent
